From 46d679e5fd00aa6807daef454225c23ac3364d38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:30:40 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 210/291] Part: headless pictures without OpenGL
 (Part.renderImage, FreeCADCmd --render)

A one-line picture from the command line, without a display, xvfb or GL:

  FreeCADCmd model.FCStd --render out.png [--view iso|front|top|...|dx,dy,dz]
             [--size 1600x1200] [--render-style shaded|shaded-only|hidden-lines|lines]

Works for anything FreeCADCmd opens (FCStd, STEP, STL ...).  Several views
(--view iso,front,top) write out_<view>.png each.

The renderer runs on the CPU (Part/App/ViewTools.cpp): the shapes are
tessellated (deflection from the size of the scene), drawn into a z-buffer
with 3x supersampling and smooth two-light shading, and edges come from
changes of face, depth jumps and creases, so outlines and silhouettes need
no extra geometry.  Meshes are split into smooth patches so STL parts look
like their CAD originals.  The PNG is written with zlib.

Python: Part.renderImage(objects, filename, view, width, height, style,
lineWidth, deflection, background, supersample) takes shapes, meshes
(points, facets), Mesh.Mesh or document objects (dicts for colours).
PartViews.render() collects the visible objects of a document (placement of
App::Part containers, links, bodies) and is what --render runs.

Tests check pixels (shaded area, edge pixels, styles), not file existence.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
